Dear Benjamin,=0D
=0D
We are thrilled to announce that in 2023 we will renew the tradition and=0D=

organize the CATchment HYdrology (CATHY) days!=0D
=0D
We would like to invite you to join our community of CATHY users and=0D
developers during an on-site event that will be held at the CENTER FOR=0D=

STUDIES ON ALPINE ENVIRONMENT in San Vito di Cadore (IT) on May 31st and=0D=

June 1st, 2023.=0D
=0D
This informal meeting will bring together researchers interested in or=0D=

working on topics connected to integrated surface-subsurface hydrological=
=0D
modeling. The meeting will be focused on a number of talks (10-20 min,=0D=

depending on the total number of contributions) that will address current=
=0D
progress and challenges in coupled surface=E2=80=93subsurface hydrologica=
l=0D
modeling, solute transport modeling, data assimilation, and catchment=0D
hydrology at large. Plus, we=E2=80=99ll make sure plenty of time is left =
for open=0D
discussion.=0D
=0D
If you are interested, please fill out the online form=0D
<https://forms.gle/c7PjrFvtcjfQtLbs7> or contact any of the organizers by=
=0D
December 23rd, including a tentative title if you would like to contribut=
e=0D
with a presentation.=0D
=0D
Respondents will receive a second announcement that will be sent out earl=
y=0D
next year with the final programme of speakers as well as information on=0D=

accommodation.=0D
=0D
=0D
There is no registration fee for the workshop; however, the number of=0D
in-person participants is *limited to 40*, due to the maximum capacity of=
=0D
the venue. Therefore, respondents will be assigned a spot on a=0D
first-come-first-serve basis. Additional respondents will be provided wit=
h=0D
a zoom link for online participation.=0D
=0D
=0D
Further details and updates will be posted on the workshop webpage=0D
<https://cathy-org.github.io/CATHY_days_2023/>. For more information, fee=
l=0D
free to contact any of us.=0D
=0D
=0D
Everyone=E2=80=99s welcome, thanks for forwarding this announcement to an=
yone who=0D
might be interested.=0D
=0D
=0D
Best,=0D
=0D
Benjamin Mary, Matteo Camporese (matteo.camporese@unipd.it), Claudio=0D
Paniconi (Claudio.Paniconi@inrs.ca), and Mario Putti (mario.putti@unipd.i=
t)=0D

